    "body": "Protected-source changes could bypass the old path-filtered release workflow. This adds three independent always-on jobs for canonical frozen-source preservation, complete isolated TeX regeneration and an actual empty historical restore in an enforced Linux network namespace.\n\nThe permanent checks protect 340 historical plus 29 accepted release files while permitting later research modules/releases. The exporter uses accepted builder/helper/manuscript bytes, the original research SHA, isolated imports and a complete 71,379-byte comparison. The archive preserves 36 refs, 26 input commits, 8,202 objects and original R evidence; offline replay checks exact objects/parents/trees, accepted verifiers, 29 old tests and original C10 consistency.\n\nReported Codex fixes reject dispatch acceptance, privilege overrides, swallowed/backgrounded/extra workflow commands, incomplete review evidence and unopened run-log ZIP substitutions. The reviewed full workflow profile is pinned; repaired-hash attacks must reach the intended semantic errors. Companion #78 also makes the archival CLI contract accurate and requires a separate actual-candidate maintenance-scope report. Its public one-time command runs on a clean checkout of actual S, joins the local result to independently captured current H/B/S, and does not restrict future research through permanent CI.\n\nExact current source:\n- H: abccf9d7ce389fffe5637ea0ff0acd5718d9058f\n- B: 37c0cb8f2fbe7934639127e5f8b6d64a01e6950f (merged #78)\n- Genuine S: 76eeb466805f229ef9fb7cd216a0d5d45c09b225\n- Tree: 965cc4973324439d46ccd8d610875c6940d7c6ab\n- Fixed accepted A: d8a4ffb5b63eb9359a4c0af9134b4f9a3c529618\n- Tooling T: cc0d29a38f3b27f4fdb760292790e677e4738d8d\n- Supplement manifest SHA-256: d6a6cc21510534f05f1006600bd47c6091c47d5228c01e6536b401d256f54a9f\n- Bundle SHA-256: 56c401a24130fd37231d667fdbad3f5578587bb6a1c6d3c406698bd5a966537f\n- ZIP: 69 entries, 7,438,442 bytes; SHA-256 a103a54501e89b014e32f0a954845e6e500bb833cac03e2ffc1320b037e75020\n\nIndependent source/package review passed at preintegration package H 3f2791d23b08d0dd157303d6c265c3dad036a349; final base-delta review, fresh S CI/C10, and actual-S scope receipt are being captured. The previous cc114 head had all nine checks green before B changed; those reports are retained as stale-evidence controls, not current acceptance.\n\nNo Lean/root, paper, release, application-schema or dependency-pin changes; zero new/changed theorem declarations or assumptions. There are 108 requirement cases (87 unit, two integration, six live PR, one review, 12 operational); actual method/subtest counts are separate. Maintenance receipts belong outside the historical supplement and its ZIP.\n\nReviewer and external publication destination remain undetermined at the user's request. The proposed ruleset stays disabled; settings/read-back, remote archival tag and external publication remain deferred. Candidate-owned code/hashes are not publisher authentication; agent/code-review evidence is not a counted approving review or mathematical peer-review certificate.",
